{
  "_about": "Orb patterns. A pattern is a list of volleys fired from the enemy's centre. Shapes: ring (count orbs around the enemy, flat unless pitch_deg), aimed (a fan of count orbs, spread_deg wide in all, toward the player), sphere (rings at pitches spread over the sky), wave (a ring along the ground: jump it). Units: speed_cms cm/s, accel_cms2 cm/s² (negative slows), min_cms and max_cms bound the speed, curl_degs turns each orb this many degrees a second (alternate: every other orb turns the other way, which draws petals), spin_deg turns the volley between repeats (a spiral), every_ms between repeats, delay_ms before the first, size_cm the orb's radius, gold orbs can be parried with Objection. aim: a ring turns to face the player first. damage (optional) overrides the default hit damage (balance.rs ORB_DAMAGE, WAVE_DAMAGE) for that volley.",
